    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The ILRS Analysis Centers weekly loose-constrained solutions used to generate the combined solution used in the ILRS contribution to ITRF2020-u2025 consists of weekly station position estimates, together with daily Earth Rotation Parameters (ERPs), namely X-pole, Y-pole, and excess Length-of-Day (LOD), estimated over 7-day arcs covering the period 2021.0\u20132026.0 and aligned with calendar weeks (Sunday to Saturday). The individual Analysis Center (AC) follow strict standards agreed upon within the ILRS Analysis Standing Committee (ASC) to provide ITRS products of the highest possible quality. NOTE: The <yymmdd> in the filenames refers to the last day of the respective week. The <x> in the file name indicates different versions of the solutions. Until September 2022, the solutions are based on observations of the four geodetic satellites LAGEOS-1, LAGEOS-2, Etalon-1, and Etalon-2. From September 2022 onwards, observations of LARES-2 are additionally included in the combined solutions.",
